  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Iris Disease through a series of indirect pathways involving other medical conditions. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone may influence the development of Iris Disease via a chain of indications, where it is linked to Autoimmune Hemolytic Anemia and Chronic Beryllium Disease, both of which are associated with Dexamethasone, a corticosteroid with anti-inflammatory properties. Dexamethasone, in turn, is linked to Iris Disease, indicating a potential role in the progression of the condition. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Prednisolone to Iris Disease highlights a possible mechanism involving systemic inflammation or immune dysregulation, though the exact nature of the relationship remains unclear. The integration of these pathways underscores the complex interplay between steroid use and ocular pathology, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the specific mechanisms by which Prednisolone may contribute to the development of Iris Disease.",
